{"timestamp": 1779356798.4117954, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 19, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779356808.769519, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I found Charlie's body in medbay. I was on my way from the lower engine and passed through storage. While I was in storage around tick 15, I clearly saw Alice walking in directly from the medbay. When I went into the medbay right after that, Charlie was lying there dead. Alice, you were just in the room where the body was, so you have a lot of explaining to do. Everyone else, please share what you know, but Alice is my top suspect right now."}}
{"timestamp": 1779356820.2557032, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Bob's timeline actually perfectly matches what I saw. I was in medbay earlier and saw Alice and Charlie walk in together around tick 12. I headed off to electrical and then security to do my tasks shortly after, leaving the two of them alone in there. If Bob saw Alice leaving medbay right before finding Charlie's body... the math kind of does itself. It really doesn't look good for Alice. I'm agreeing with Bob on this one, I think we have to vote Alice."}}
{"timestamp": 1779356836.7420573, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Bob, I understand why I look suspicious from your perspective since you saw me leaving medbay right before you found the body, but you need to listen carefully because Eve is lying to frame me. \n\nAt tick 13, I was in medbay with BOTH Eve and Charlie. I finished what I was doing and left them there to go down to storage, which is exactly why you saw me enter storage at tick 15. I was with you in storage from ticks 15 to 17! \n\nEve is completely twisting the facts. I didn't stay in medbay with Charlie; I left *Eve* alone with Charlie. She killed him the second I walked out, and now she's jumping on your suspicion to get an easy misvote. There is only one Duck left in this game, and Eve's blatant lie proves it's her. We need to vote Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779356868.1668382, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I've been on the far left side of the map this entire round. My route was oxygen, then upper engine, and I just arrived at lower engine before the meeting. I haven't encountered a single person all game. Bob, you mentioned you were on your way from the lower engine to storage, but I never saw you\u2014though it's possible we just barely missed each other depending on the exact ticks.\n\nWhat we have here is a definitive 1v1 between Alice and Eve. They are directly contradicting each other about who left who alone with Charlie in medbay. One of them is lying and is undeniably the last Duck.\n\nPersonally, Eve is setting off massive alarm bells for me. First, she's the one who reported Frank's body back in the first meeting at tick 11. Now, for this second body, she is instantly agreeing with Bob's theory to lock in a vote on Alice. It feels incredibly opportunistic\u2014a classic Duck move to let an innocent player (Bob) cast suspicion, and then jump on it to secure the misvote. \n\nMeanwhile, Alice's defense is extremely specific. She claims she was with Bob in storage from ticks 15 to 17. If she's lying about that, she knows Bob would immediately know she's lying, which is a huge risk for a Duck to take when defending themselves.\n\nSince there are only 4 of us left and 1 Duck, a wrong vote right now loses us the game. We can't afford to be wrong. However, because of the direct contradiction, the Duck has to be Alice or Eve. I strongly believe Eve's opportunistic bandwagoning and previous report point to her being the killer trying to close out the game. I am voting Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779356887.221735, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Hold on, everyone. Alice is actually telling the exact truth. I was so focused on seeing her come from the medbay that I didn't emphasize the rest of the timeline\u2014she *was* with me in storage from tick 15 all the way to 17. \n\nSince Alice was with me in storage for those ticks, she couldn't have killed Charlie right before I walked into medbay. Eve, your story completely falls apart here. You jumped way too fast on my initial suspicion to try and secure a misvote on Alice. Diana is completely right about this being a 1v1, and given that I can confirm Alice's alibi in storage, Eve has to be the last Duck. We are voting Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779356915.031906, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Diana, Alice, please take a step back and look at exactly what Bob is doing here. Yes, I initially agreed with Bob's theory about Alice because, from my perspective, it made perfect sense! I left Alice and Charlie in medbay at tick 13. When Bob said he saw Alice leaving and found Charlie dead right after, I genuinely thought Alice was the killer. \n\nBut now Bob is suddenly backpedaling and heavily confirming Alice's alibi in storage. Why? Because Bob is the Duck. Think about it: Bob is the one who found the body. He likely walked into medbay, killed Charlie himself, and self-reported. He realized that if he pushed Alice too hard, he'd be in a 1v1 with her. Instead, he\u2019s strategically \"clearing\" Alice to pocket her and guarantee she votes with him against me. \n\nAlice, he is using you. He needed an accomplice to force a misvote, and by clearing you, he knows you'll blindly trust him. Diana, you said a wrong vote loses us the game. Bob orchestrated this entire narrative to pit us against each other while keeping his own hands clean. I am voting Bob, and you both need to see through his manipulation before it's too late."}}
{"timestamp": 1779356937.788929, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Eve, that is the most desperate pivot I have ever seen. You got caught in a massive lie, and now you're just throwing accusations at the wall to see what sticks. \n\nLet's look at the facts: I *know* you were in medbay with Charlie at tick 13, because I was literally standing right there with both of you before I walked down to storage. You lied and claimed you left at tick 12 to frame me. You thought you had a free kill and an easy misvote because Bob happened to see me leaving the area. \n\nIf Bob were actually the Duck, he had absolutely no reason to backtrack. He had your full support to vote me out! He could have just stuck to his original story, taken your vote, and won the game for the Ducks right then and there. Instead, he stopped, realized he actually *was* with me in storage from ticks 15 to 17, and cleared me. That is exactly what an innocent player does when they reconstruct the timeline. \n\nDiana, you nailed it earlier. Eve tried to opportunistically bandwagon onto Bob's suspicion to get me ejected. Now that Bob has ruined her frame job by confirming my alibi, she's panicking and calling him the mastermind. Don't let her confuse you. Eve is the last Duck, and we have her dead to rights. I am voting Eve, and you should both do the same so we can win this."}}
{"timestamp": 1779356958.014003, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Alice is completely right here about the mechanics of this situation. If Bob were the Duck, he had absolutely no reason to backtrack and clear Alice. Eve had already handed him the perfect misvote on a silver platter! If Bob were the Duck, all he had to do was stick to his original accusation, take Eve's vote against Alice, and he would have essentially won the game right there. \n\nInstead, Bob stopped, reviewed his own memory of the timeline, and realized Alice was with him in storage. That is the behavior of an innocent player trying to get the facts straight, not a Duck trying to force a win. \n\nEve, your attempt to suddenly paint Bob as a mastermind manipulating Alice is incredibly desperate. You lied about the timeline to frame Alice, and when Bob's memory proved you wrong, you panicked and changed your target. \n\nI'm sticking to my original read from earlier. Eve is the Duck, and she's out of options. Let's vote Eve and end this."}}
